-- Customer & Basic Analysis
-- SELECT – SmartBank wants to maintain a customer directory. Display complete details of all registered customers.
-- DISTINCT – Management wants to know the different cities from which SmartBank customers are coming. Display the unique customer cities.
-- WHERE – Identify all customers whose current status is Active.
-- AND – Find active customers who are currently registered in Mumbai.
-- OR – Find customers registered in either Mumbai or Pune.
-- NOT – Identify customers who are registered in cities other than Mumbai.
-- BETWEEN – Find customers whose age falls between 30 and 50 years for customer demographic analysis.
-- IN – Identify customers belonging to Mumbai, Pune, Nashik, or Nagpur.
-- LIKE – Find customers whose names begin with the letter A.
-- IS NULL – Identify customers whose email address is not available in the bank records.
-- IS NOT NULL – Identify customers who have a registered email address.
-- ORDER BY – Display customer accounts from highest to lowest balance to identify high-value accounts.
-- LIMIT – Identify the top 5 accounts with the highest balance for priority customer analysis.

